name: sim.scaleObjects
description: Scales specified objects. All related values are automatically scaled appropriately (e.g. masses, forces, etc.)
luaSynopsis: sim.scaleObjects(list objectHandles, float scalingFactor, bool scalePositionsToo)
pythonSynopsis: sim.scaleObjects(int[] objectHandles, float scalingFactor, bool scalePositionsToo)
inputs:
1. objectHandles: array containing the handles of the objects to scale. If an object is a model base, all its child objects will also be scaled
2. scalingFactor: scaling factor
3. scalePositionsToo: if true, selected object's positions will also be scaled
outputs:
